<title>USA: Loewen Group may issue $350 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Loewen Group may issue $350 mln in debt.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Sept 27 - Loewen Group Inc is expected to issue $350 million in debt in a two-part private placement deal sometime next week, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The deal consists of $175 million in five-year debt and $175 million in seven-year debt, sources added.</p>
<p>The issue is expected to be led by Smith Barney.</p>
<p>No further details on the pricing were available.</p>
<p>Service Corp International has made a takeover bid for Loewen.</p>
<p>- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
